venezuelan colombian edward castrillon  was doing his job in bogota recently  when he was stopped by the police for a  routine check he was dumbfounded when he  was told his colombian id was fake and  was arrested for 36 hours  i was in shock because i was sure i had  done nothing wrong they still handcuffed  me and took me to the police station  edward was born in venezuela but having  a colombian mother he was able to get  citizenship when he migrated here in  2019  but now he says he's living in a limbo  fearing he could end up in jail again  every time he leaves the house  a right to my identity has been violated  yes i was born in venezuela but already  have a life here a credit history  everything now i live in fear feeling  that i am some sort of criminal  and edward is not alone 43 000  venezuelan colombian citizens have lost  their ids in the last few weeks  colombia's national registry says they  found irregularities in their  documentation as part of a purging of  the electoral census their ids were  cancelled and the majority were not  notified since then more than 200 have  been arrested and others have had severe  consequences  the director of the civil registry says  that while the difficulty many faced are  unfortunate they had no option given the  fact the records show some irregularity  it's the mechanism we have in our  country to integrate people effectively  into the rule of law that will give them  all the guarantees that correspond to  them as colombian citizens but the  adjustment to the law is inevitably  applicable  but some suspect darker motives they say  the so-called irregularities could be an  excuse used by the government to reduce  the participation in upcoming  presidential elections of citizens  linked to socialist venezuelan  others claim it's the government's  heavy-handed response to allegations of  fake ids circulating in the country  whatever the reason it's having an  impact  who runs a human rights foundation that  assists venezuelan migrants has gathered  almost 5 000 wrongful cases  these people is colombian we are  colombian and every administrative  decision that you take affects the life  of these people today we have people  that have cancer and are not receiving  their treatment because these situations  leaving many to face the real life  consequences of bureaucratic decisions  beyond their control  alessandra ampietti al jazeera bogota
 

